prs.body:
Fixes https://github.com/tc39/ecma262/issues/3978. That was closed because it was opened by an LLM without permission but it really is a bug, observable with

```js
let rab = new ArrayBuffer(16, { maxByteLength: 16 });
let ta = new BigInt64Array(rab);

ta.with(0, { valueOf() { rab.resize(8); return 0n; } });
```
and
```js
let rab = new ArrayBuffer(16, { maxByteLength: 16 });
let ta = new BigInt64Array(rab);

ta.filter(() => { rab.resize(8); return true; });
```
and
```js
let rab = new ArrayBuffer(16);
let ta = new BigInt64Array(rab);

ta.filter(() => { if (!rab.detached) rab.transfer(); return true; });
```

Bug report didn't mention detaching but it comes up for `filter`; afaict it does not for `with` (because the coercions happen before the `IsValidIntegerIndex` check, which always returns false for detached buffers).
